{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q016_pdb_1acc_domain_split","answer":"In SCOP 1.75, chain A of PDB 1acc was one domain, d1acca_ (SUNID 43828), covering “A:” and classified as family f.11.1.1 in the Anthrax protective antigen superfamily/fold. Stable SCOPe 2.07 and 2.08 instead contain two domains: the N-terminal d1acca2 (SUNID 238522; A:14-225), family b.179.1.1 “PA14,” superfamily b.179.1 “PA14-like,” fold b.179, all-beta class b; and the C-terminal d1acca1 (SUNID 238521; A:226-735), family f.60.1.1, superfamily f.60.1, and fold f.60 “Anthrax protective antigen C-terminal-like,” in class f. Thus the former whole-chain domain was replaced by two adjacent, separately classified regions; residues outside the reported ranges are not assigned to either retrieved domain.

Biologically, this illustrates that a PDB chain is not necessarily one evolutionary unit. Separately classifiable domains can be combined in one protein and recognized in other evolutionary contexts. SCOPe supports family/superfamily homology searches separately for the PA14-like N-terminal module and the C-terminal-like module. Because these two modules have different classes, folds, and superfamilies, SCOPe makes no homology assertion between them—but that alone does not prove convergence or independent origin.

Homology searches should therefore use residues 14-225 and 226-735 as separate queries or apply domain-aware methods. A hit to one region supports a relationship only for that module: it must not be extended automatically to the other domain or to the complete protective-antigen chain. Likewise, toxin/protective-antigen function, calcium binding, receptor specificity, reaction or ligand specificity, oligomeric behavior, and whole-protein architecture cannot be transferred from a domain-level match alone. A structure matched to one module is not automatically an interchangeable full-chain template. Such conclusions require residue-resolved sequence and structural alignments, coverage and topology assessment, conserved functional residues in equivalent contexts, ligand-bound or biochemical evidence, compatible domain architecture, and where relevant phylogenetic or literature support. The retrieved API records establish that the split occurred but do not expose the curator’s alignment or literature rationale. No structural-quality comparison was retrieved, so they also do not select a best representative.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry — /api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc; /api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.07/pdb/1acc; /api/v1/releases/2.07/pdb/1acc/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc/domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains — /api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_; /api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2/parents"]}]}
